1
00:00:00,950 --> 00:00:03,270
This is Memory Monster.

2
00:00:03,830 --> 00:00:09,270
When your memory fills up, a door opens, and a dark figure steps out.

3
00:00:09,470 --> 00:00:13,030
A real system monitor shows this computer's memory.

4
00:00:13,150 --> 00:00:16,810
Memory Monster reads the same numbers, and waits.

5
00:00:17,090 --> 00:00:21,450
The line is set low, so a quiet computer can show you.

6
00:00:21,570 --> 00:00:24,930
Now something big starts eating memory.

7
00:00:24,970 --> 00:00:27,230
Watch the monitor, and the door.

8
00:00:27,370 --> 00:00:32,710
Past the line, the door opens wide, and he steps out.

9
00:00:39,770 --> 00:00:43,550
Then the monitor drops, and he goes back behind the door.

10
00:00:50,070 --> 00:00:53,290
That is Shadow Form, the default look.

11
00:00:53,510 --> 00:00:55,690
Every look has its own entrance.

12
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,070
Same memory, different monster.

13
00:00:58,170 --> 00:01:03,390
Green Visitor: an alien in a top hat, dropping out of a glowing portal.

14
00:01:07,450 --> 00:01:10,480
The Detective, in a trench coat.

15
00:01:10,510 --> 00:01:14,350
His metal door slides open, and he slides in.

16
00:01:17,870 --> 00:01:21,330
The Ghost, with a pale mask and a cloak.

17
00:01:21,410 --> 00:01:25,030
A curtain parts, and he rises up from the floor.

18
00:01:26,870 --> 00:01:33,110
Night Shift: a hoodie, a glowing grin, and he walks out of a wooden door.

19
00:01:38,470 --> 00:01:40,930
Close the program, and he goes home.

20
00:01:41,670 --> 00:01:45,890
Make him yours: pick a look, or edit one small file.

